-- title:
--   Closed two-sided ideal generated by an element of a unital $C^*$-algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a unital $C^*$-algebra and let $v\in A$.
--
--   1. **Ideal words.** The two-sided multiples of $v$ form the set
--
--      $$
--      W(v)=\{\,xvy \;:\; x,y\in A\,\}.
--      $$
--
--      Since $A$ has a unit, $W(v)$ contains $v$, $av$ and $va$ for every $a\in A$.
--
--   2. **Algebraic ideal.** $I_0(v)=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{C}}W(v)$ is the complex linear span of the ideal words, i.e. the algebraic two-sided ideal of $A$ generated by $v$. It is closed under left multiplication by arbitrary elements of $A$, because $a(xvy)=(ax)vy$. If $v$ is self-adjoint it is also closed under the adjoint, because $(xvy)^*=y^*vx^*$; so for self-adjoint $v$, $I_0(v)$ is a (non-unital) $*$-subalgebra of $A$.
--
--   3. **Closed ideal.** For self-adjoint $v$,
--
--      $$
--      J(v)=\overline{I_0(v)}=\overline{\operatorname{span}}\,\{\,xvy \;:\; x,y\in A\,\}
--      $$
--
--      is the norm closure of $I_0(v)$, the closed two-sided ideal of $A$ generated by $v$. It is a closed, hence complete, $*$-subalgebra of $A$, and therefore a $C^*$-algebra in its own right.
--
--   The closed ideal $J(v)$ is where comparison with $v$ takes place. In the surrounding development it is shown that if $v$ is positive and properly infinite (the diagonal matrix $\operatorname{diag}(v,v)$ is a norm limit of products $r_j^*vr_j$ with row vectors $r_j\in A^{1\times 2}$), then every positive $u\in J(v)$ is a norm limit of elements $w^*vw$ with $w\in A$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The Lean names are `idealWords v` (a set), `idealSpan v` (a complex submodule of `A`), and `idealAlgebra v hv` and `closedIdeal v hv` (non-unital star subalgebras; the latter is the `topologicalClosure` of the former). The last two take a proof `hv` that $v$ is self-adjoint. The file also proves `idealSpan_word`, `idealSpan_left`, `idealSpan_star` and `closedIdeal_closed`, and registers completeness of `closedIdeal v hv` as an instance (`closedIdeal_complete`).
